{
  "title": "iOS full-recipe cache for local search",
  "description": "Offline iOS search needs a complete local search document. \
The current CoreData cache stores only `RecipeSummary` fields, while bare-text \
server matching also uses ingredients, instructions, and notes, and relevance \
ranking additionally uses tags. See doc/local-recipe-search-and-sync.md for \
the decided storage and parity contracts.\n\
\n\
Scope when unblocked:\n\
- Extend the existing recipe sync/cache path with the purpose-specific search \
document, including structured ingredient scorer inputs and the exact \
server-produced `ingredients::text` match value.\n\
- Preserve the narrow read-only cache design; do not turn this into full \
local-first/offline-write storage.\n\
- Keep web server-side unless product scope changes; web does not need an \
offline recipe corpus.\n\
- Add API and iOS tests for initial population, updates, tag changes, \
soft-delete tombstones, normalization-contract versions, and every field \
needed by local matching and ranking.\n\
- Measure initial payload size, stored cache size, and sync duration against a \
representative large cookbook.\n\
\n\
This is the cache dependency for blocked-ios-local-search-relevance.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
